      "topic": "Multiple testing",
      "judgment": "All gene tables correctly apply BH across 21117 genes separately per declared contrast and branch. CAMERA FDR is per library/contrast/branch; FDR_across_four_contrasts is an additional BH within a library and branch across four contrasts. It is not a single experiment-wide FDR across libraries, branches and all exploratory hypotheses."
    },
    {
      "topic": "CAMERA interpretation",
      "judgment": "CAMERA is a competitive gene-set test with fixed inter-gene correlation 0.01 and use.ranks=FALSE. It measures coordinated relative transcriptional association versus the assayed background under that correlation assumption. Direction does not establish functional pathway activity, cell-intrinsic state, causal drug specificity, barrier restoration, or a new cell population. Coherent small effects can yield gene-set significance when no individual gene passes BH."
    },
